        "## 23.25 Worked calculation\n",
        "\n",
        "Consider the undirected path graph with three nodes:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "1-2-3.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The adjacency matrix is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A=\\begin{bmatrix}\n",
        "0 & 1 & 0\\\\\n",
        "1 & 0 & 1\\\\\n",
        "0 & 1 & 0\n",
        "\\end{bmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The degree matrix is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "D=\\begin{bmatrix}\n",
        "1 & 0 & 0\\\\\n",
        "0 & 2 & 0\\\\\n",
        "0 & 0 & 1\n",
        "\\end{bmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The Laplacian is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "L=D-A=\n",
        "\\begin{bmatrix}\n",
        "1 & -1 & 0\\\\\n",
        "-1 & 2 & -1\\\\\n",
        "0 & -1 & 1\n",
        "\\end{bmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "For a signal $f=(1,0,-1)^T$,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "Lf = (1,0,-1)^T,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "so\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "f^TLf = 2.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Using the edge formula gives\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "(1-0)^2 + (0-(-1))^2 = 2.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Thus the Laplacian energy equals the sum of squared differences over undirected edges.\n",
